time required: 12 hours 30 minutes
alternative_name: Slow Cooker Apple Butter
ingredient_count: 7
---

Place the @apples{6 1/2%pounds}(peeled, cored and sliced) in a #slow cooker{}. In a #medium bowl{}, combine @granulated sugar{1%cup}, @light brown sugar{1%cup}(lightly packed), @ground cinnamon{1%tablespoon}, @freshly grated nutmeg{1/2%teaspoon}, @ground cloves{1/4%teaspoon} and @salt{1/4%teaspoon}. Pour the mixture over the apples and mix well.

Cook in slow cooker on low for about ~{10%hours}, stirring occasionally, until the mixture is thickened and dark brown.

Uncover, stir in @pure vanilla extract{1%tablespoon} and continue cooking uncovered on low for about ~{2%hours}.

Use an #immersion blender{} to puree the apple butter until smooth.

Spoon the mixture into sterile #containers{}, cover and refrigerate for up to two weeks or freeze.

> Serve on breads, muffins, pork chops or just eat it with a spoon.